IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 1 (PART): APPLICATION OF THE ACT.
--
--   "Does the Act apply to this tenancy, and do the market rent and periodic
--    notice sections apply to it?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 5, 7, 8.

§ `Application of the Act`

-- s 5(1) "This Act shall not apply in the following cases: (a) where the
-- premises are commercial premises: ..." (the list is an input, one
-- constructor per paragraph). s 8(1) "Nothing in any of sections 5 to 7 shall
-- prevent the parties to a tenancy that would otherwise be excluded ... from
-- agreeing in writing that all or any of the provisions of this Act shall
-- apply".
@ref ss 5, 8
@export Whether the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ) applies to a tenancy: unless one of the s 5 exclusions applies (commercial premises, a hotel, holiday premises, a landlord's own home, and the rest of s 5), or the parties to an excluded tenancy agreed in writing that it applies (s 8). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A Tenancy  @desc Which s 5 exclusion applies (if any), whether the parties agreed in writing that the Act applies, and the length of any fixed term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` t IF
        t's `exclusion` EQUALS `none of the s 5 exclusions`
    OR  t's `the parties agreed in writing that the Act applies`

-- s 7 "(1) ... nothing in sections 25 to 28 and 51 shall apply to a tenancy
-- for a fixed term of not more than 90 days (whether or not terminable by
-- notice) if, before the commencement of the tenancy, the parties agree in
-- writing that the tenancy will not be extended or renewed to give a total
-- length of the term in excess of 90 days. (2) Where such a tenancy is
-- extended or renewed ... with the result that the total length of the term
-- exceeds 90 days, on the expiry of that period of 90 days the tenancy shall
-- become subject to sections 25 to 28 and 51".
@ref s 7(1)-(2)
@export Whether ss 25-28 (market rent) and 51 (termination by notice) of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ) apply to a tenancy: not to a fixed term of no more than 90 days agreed in writing beforehand not to run beyond 90 days, unless extensions take its total length over 90 days (s 7). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A Tenancy  @desc The fixed term (if any), the written agreement not to extend, and the total term after extensions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` t IF
    NOT (    short
         AND t's `agreed in writing not to extend beyond 90 days`
         AND t's `total term after any extension or renewal, in days` AT MOST 90)
    WHERE
        short MEANS
            CONSIDER t's `fixed term, in days, if any`
            WHEN JUST n THEN n AT MOST 90
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
